¥fauthorxApub:sha2-256:ue7bjgletvpfendw4dptudm64oaaqaoia3pu7vnao6xq6fq5o6jqdbody§eclassldefinitionalgcontentx<The PDC classes directly under --- COMMON AUXILIARY NUMBERS.gdefines¤hgroupinggmembers†¥hboundary¢hexcludes€hincludesyIThe common auxiliaries of time denote the date, point of time or range of time of a subject represented by a main UDC number. The basis of date indication is the Christian calendar, but non-Christian systems of time reckoning are also allowed for (in "68" and "69"), as well as other time concepts, e.g. seasons and geologic timehchildrenõgmatches¢crefxhttp://udcdata.info/011472hrelationeexactdnamex$Common auxiliaries of time. Table 1gcpdce"..."¥hboundary¢hexcludes€hincludesxÆThe common auxiliaries of form denote the form or presentation of documents. They are not used to denote the subject matter of documents. For literary forms (poetry, plays, fiction etc.) see 82-1/-9hchildrenõgmatches¢crefxhttp://udcdata.info/001585hrelationeexactdnamex$Common auxiliaries of form. Table 1dcpdcf(0...)¥hboundary¢hexcludes€hincludesyEThe place auxiliaries indicate the geographical range, locality or other spatial aspect of a subject denoted by a main UDC number, e.g. 331.2(44) Wages in France, 338.47(81) Economics of transport in Brazil. Most importantly, place auxiliaries are the primary facet in the subdivision of 913 Regional geography and 94 Historyhchildrenõgmatches¢crefxhttp://udcdata.info/001951hrelationeexactdnamex%Common auxiliaries of place. Table 1ecpdce(1/9)¥hboundary¢hexcludes€hincludesy‚The common auxiliaries of ethnic grouping and nationality denote the nationality or ethnic aspects of a subject represented by a main UDC number. They are derived mainly from the common auxiliaries of language =... (Table 1c) and so may also usefully distinguish linguistic-cultural groups, e.g. (=111) English speaking peoples. For special anthropogeography as a main subject see 572.9hchildrenõgmatches¢crefxhttp://udcdata.info/011755hrelationeexactdnamexOCommon auxiliaries of human ancestry, ethnic grouping and nationality. Table 1fcpdcf(=...)¤hchildrenõgmatches¢crefxhttp://udcdata.info/011791hrelationeexactdnamexpCommon auxiliaries of general characteristics: Properties, Materials, Relations/Processes and Persons. Table 1k.cpdce-0...¥hboundary¢hexcludes€hincludesy—The common auxiliaries of language denote the language or linguistic form of a document whose subject is denoted by a main UDC number. Table 1c is the main place in the UDC tables for enumeration of languages, and serves as the source for the subdivision of Class 811 Languages (as subjects of study), Class 821 Literatures of individual languages, and (=...) Common auxiliaries of ethnic grouping, Table 1fhchildrenõgmatches¢crefxhttp://udcdata.info/000008hrelationeexactdnamex(Common auxiliaries of language. Table 1ccpdcd=...fparentc---dsortffamilygdepends€hevidence¤dkindhexternaldnotex)UDC Summary, UDC Consortium, CC BY-SA 3.0crefx9https://api.finto.fi/rest/v1/udcs/data?format=text/turtledrolehcitationdlangbenescope¢jconditions€fdomainmunconditionalgcreatedt2026-11-03T07:28:11Zcpuba1dtypekclaim.prose